  "enisaUuid": "151e4092-461d-36ca-abb6-e222cb9a0f38",
  "description": "A vulnerability was identified in D\u00edgitro NGC Explorer up to 3.48.21. The affected element is an unknown function of the component Configuration Page. Such manipulation leads to missing password field masking. It is possible to launch the attack remotely. Upgrading to version 3.48.22 is sufficient to fix this issue. It is suggested to upgrade the affected component. The action taken by the vendor is: \"Review and correction of controls related to the exposure of user information in the product configuration interface.\" The vulnerabilities are limited to NGC Explorer and do not affect other D\u00edgitro products, including UNA and Guardi\u00e3o.",
